  "version": "other",
  "operative_text": "(a_in_person_id) not stated.\n(b_no_id_remedy) not stated.\n(c_mail_ballot_id) not stated.\n(d_proof_of_citizenship) not stated.\n(e_other_rule) not stated.\n(other) 3501.055 (new): election integrity unit in the secretary of state's office; investigates election fraud and voter suppression allegations (not 3599.03 or 3599.031), takes public allegations, refers cases, reports yearly, may subpoena; prosecutors must act on referrals within one year or explain.\n(other) 3501.05: amended to match (the introduced version also changed attorney general prosecution authority in section 109.95; later versions drop that).\n(other) version: 00_IN, 01_RS, 02_PS: no ID or citizenship text in any version. 00_IN also amends attorney general prosecutorial authority (109.95); 01_RS and 02_PS drop it and keep the election integrity unit.\n(other) note: Election integrity unit bill. The only mentions of voter identification or citizenship are existing duties in R.C. 3501.05 reprinted unchanged (voter education on ID; Uniformed and Overseas Citizens Absentee Voting Act). Passed the Senate only; the House referred it to committee.\n(note) Off this topic: the bill sets no ID or citizenship-proof rule.",
